course: dictionary
lesson: 557
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning the writer means. «Potatoes are cousins of tomatoes, peppers and aubergines» is about food, because tomatoes and peppers are vegetables, so an aubergine must be one too.
explain: Aubergine can also be a colour. A dark purple colour is called aubergine, so you can have an aubergine scarf. Ask yourself: is this about cooking or eating? Then it means the vegetable. Is it about clothes, paint or what something looks like? Then it means the colour.
explain: Where you live can change the name. In the UK and Ireland, this vegetable is called an aubergine. In the USA, Canada and Australia, people say eggplant. Both words mean the same vegetable, so a recipe that says eggplant is talking about the same food.
fact: An aubergine is a vegetable with smooth, shiny, dark purple skin and soft white flesh inside.
fact: In the USA, Canada and Australia, an aubergine is called an eggplant.
fact: «Aubergine» can also mean a dark purple colour.
fact: Moussaka, ratatouille and baba ghanoush are dishes that use aubergine.
fact: Aubergine is a noun for the vegetable, and it can also be an adjective that describes a colour, as in an aubergine scarf.
exercise: «Potatoes are cousins of tomatoes, peppers and aubergines.» What is an aubergine in this sentence? | *A vegetable | A small bird | A dark purple colour | A type of bread
exercise: Mum says, «Add the aubergine to the pan with the onions.» What is the aubergine? | *A vegetable you can cook | A kind of spoon | A tall tree | A colour of a pan
exercise: In the USA, a recipe says «Slice one eggplant.» What is an eggplant? | A kind of cheese | *An aubergine, the same vegetable | A purple fruit that grows on trees | A cooking pot
test: Sam says, «I love moussaka, and it has aubergine in it.» What is aubergine in this sentence? | A type of shoe | A piece of music | A blue dog | *A vegetable
test: Which dish from the lesson uses aubergine? | Toast | Pancakes | *Ratatouille | Fish and chips
exam: What does aubergine mean in «Mum bought two aubergines for the moussaka»? | A type of cake | A long, thin fish | *A vegetable | A dark purple colour
